https://abhishek439dev.github.io/MERN-Stack-Codes/CSS/Grids

CSS Grids is a tool to create 2D layouts of complex shapes. These layouts are somewhat responsive as well. 
We can apply CSS grids to a number of divs by setting display property to grid. 
.container{
  display: grid;
}

Now, we have to define the number of rows and columns we require in our layout using.
grid-template-rows and grid-template-column
.container{
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr 2 fr;
  grid-template-column: 1fr 1fr;
}

We can set a fixed size(in px or em or rem) or fractional sizes(1fr or 1.5fr or 2 fr) as well. Fractional units make the divs responsive to screen size change.
We can also use a function, repeat(6, 1fr); to create more number of tracks quickly. 
.container{
  display: grid;
  grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr 2 fr;
  grid-template-column: repeat(2, 1fr);
}

After this we have to set the area for our components in the grid.
.div1{
  grid-rows: 1 / 2;
  grid-column: 1 / 3;
}

we can also use span keyword to span the number of cells in the grid.
.div2{
  grid-rows: 1 / 2;
  grid-column: span 2;  /*[start from its position(or we can specify it) and span two cells].*/
}
